# Generated by `node tools/polestar.js profession draft Engineering --out` from Forever's client tables, trainer lists and data/forever. Do not edit: rebuild with that command.
guide forever/professions/engineering
title Engineering 1-300
category Professions
levels 5-60
zone Azeroth

# Engineering builds bombs, guns, goggles, scopes and gadgets from parts it makes itself: blasting
# powder from stone, bolts and tubes from bars. Mining is its partner. Keep a Blacksmith Hammer and
# the Arclight Spanner (made at 57) in your bags; most recipes need an anvil. Goggles and scopes
# also want a Gyromatic Micro-Adjustor (from 175, 4 Steel Bars), which this route never needs.
#
# Forever's changes: the colours and learn skills are Classic's, so a Classic order works, but
# Gnomes no longer get +15 Engineering (Forever's client changed the racial). A few reagents changed
# (Rough Dynamite takes one powder; EZ-Thro Dynamite needs an EZ-Thro Wrap). New SAF-T and EZ-Thro
# schematics are sold for Merchant's Favor by Fizzlefuse near the Crossroads and Fritz Fizzle at
# Three Corners (Redridge); Sandpaper (Bauxite from Gold Veins) feeds blacksmiths' plans. Merchant's
# Favor is a currency from the supply crates turned in at the camps, not gold; its patterns bind
# when picked up. Many late schematics (Thorium Tube, Accurate Scope, Deadly Scope) now bind when
# picked up.
#
# Camping: Reagent Bot (skill 20) is the Engineering camp item; you learn it at 20 but its parts
# come at 30 and 50, so it gives no points. The Repair Bot (skill 140) comes from a blueprint Sneed
# drops in the Deadmines; the skill-300 Anarchist's Workbench has no known source.
#
# Ranks: trainers teach by tier and train only from their tier's skill: Journeyman at the city
# trainers, from skill 50; Expert only at Springspindle Fizzlegear (Ironforge) and Roxxik
# (Orgrimmar), from 125; Artisan only at Buzzek Bracketswing (Gadgetzan), from 200. Specialisation
# at 200 and level 30: Gnomish (Tinkmaster Overspark, Ironforge / Oglethorpe Obnoticus, Booty Bay)
# or Goblin (Nixx Sprocketspring, Gadgetzan).
#
# Route (crafts are expected counts; yellow and green crafts can take more):
#     1-35  Rough Blasting Powder, about 46 (known): 1 Rough Stone each
#    35-57  Handful of Copper Bolts, about 33 (trainer 1s 15c): 1 Copper Bar each
#    57-75  Copper Tube, about 18 (trainer 1s 50c): 2 Copper Bar and 1 Weak Flux each
#    75-94  Crafted Heavy Shot, about 15 (trainer 2s 50c): 1 Coarse Blasting Powder and 1 Copper Bar each
#    94-100 Copper Tube, about 14 (trainer 1s 50c): 2 Copper Bar and 1 Weak Flux each
#   100-125 Practice Lock, about 31 (trainer): 1 Bronze Bar, 2 Handful of Copper Bolts and 1 Weak Flux each
#   125-140 Heavy Blasting Powder, about 27 (trainer): 1 Heavy Stone each
#   140-150 Big Bronze Bomb, about 10 (trainer): 2 Heavy Blasting Powder, 3 Bronze Bar and 1 Silver Contact each
#   150-166 Aquadynamic Fish Attractor, about 31 (trainer): 2 Bronze Bar, 1 Nightcrawlers and 1 Coarse Blasting Powder each
#   166-175 Bronze Framework, about 19 (trainer): 2 Bronze Bar, 1 Medium Leather and 1 Wool Cloth each
#   175-191 Solid Blasting Powder, about 31 (trainer): 2 Solid Stone each
#   191-210 Big Iron Bomb, about 27 (trainer): 3 Iron Bar, 3 Heavy Blasting Powder and 1 Silver Contact each
#   210-225 Hi-Impact Mithril Slugs, about 19 (trainer): 1 Mithril Bar and 1 Solid Blasting Powder each
#   225-245 Hi-Impact Mithril Slugs, about 62 (trainer): 1 Mithril Bar and 1 Solid Blasting Powder each
#   245-265 Mithril Gyro-Shot, about 28 (trainer): 2 Mithril Bar and 2 Solid Blasting Powder each
#   265-287 Thorium Widget, about 24 (recipe 1g 20s): 3 Thorium Bar and 1 Runecloth each
#   287-300 Thorium Tube, about 14 (recipe 1g 60s): 6 Thorium Bar each
#
# Shopping per bracket (vendor goods at vendor prices; gathered or dropped materials by count):
# 1-75: Apprentice 10c, recipes 4s 15c, vendor goods 18s 18c; gather or buy 46 Rough Stone and 75
# Copper Bar.
# 75-150: Journeyman 5s (Classic price), recipes 5s plus unpriced trainer recipes, vendor goods 45s;
# gather or buy 15 Coarse Stone, 27 Heavy Stone, 72 Copper Bar, 61 Bronze Bar and 2 Silver Bar.
# 150-225: Expert 50s (Classic price), trainer recipes (prices not in the data), vendor goods 31s;
# gather or buy 19 Medium Leather, 19 Wool Cloth, 31 Coarse Stone, 74 Heavy Stone, 100 Bronze Bar, 6
# Silver Bar, 81 Iron Bar, 19 Mithril Bar and 62 Solid Stone.
# 225-300: Artisan 4g 50s (Classic price), recipes 2g 80s plus unpriced trainer recipes; gather or
# buy 118 Mithril Bar, 212 Solid Stone, 156 Thorium Bar and 24 Runecloth.
#
# Data: recipes, colours and reagents from the Forever client's tables; trainer learn skills and
# prices from Forever's sniffed trainer lists (they reach skill 50-150); vendors, stock and drops
# from data/forever. Materials are valued at about four times their vendor sell price (cloth and
# leather by the square root of it, hides four times higher; tools/lib/professions/materials.js) to
# rank recipes against each other, never as a price forecast.
# ASSUMED: learn skills of Practice Lock 100, Heavy Blasting Powder 125, Silver Contact 90, Big
# Bronze Bomb 140, Aquadynamic Fish Attractor 150, Bronze Framework 145, Solid Blasting Powder 175,
# Big Iron Bomb 190, Hi-Impact Mithril Slugs 210 and Mithril Gyro-Shot 245 (no sniffed Forever list
# teaches them: Classic's trainer skill moved as far as Forever moved the recipe's colours, which
# the sniffed lists bear out on 126 of 129 recipes). In-game check: the skill the trainer asks;
# their prices are not in the data.
# ASSUMED: rank level gates Journeyman 10, Expert 20 and Artisan 35 (Classic's; Forever's sniffed
# lists ask level 1 for Apprentice). In-game check: the level each trainer asks.
# ASSUMED: rank prices Journeyman 5s, Expert 50s and Artisan 4g 50s (Classic's trainer lists and
# Forever's Blacksmithing ranks; Forever's sniffed lists price only Apprentice, 10c as in Classic).
# In-game check: what each rank costs.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Apprentice (1-75)
section Engineering 1-75

step Learn Engineering
  tip Apprentice Engineering lets you craft up to 75 for 10c, at any character level. Any Engineering trainer of your faction teaches it; the arrow picks the nearest. Buy a Blacksmith Hammer and pair it with Mining: Rough Stone and Copper Ore are the first parts. 1-75 takes about 4s 15c of recipes and 18s 18c of vendor goods, plus 46 Rough Stone and 75 Copper Bar to gather or buy.
  train Engineering Apprentice
  skill Engineering 1

step Engineering 1-75: vendor goods
  tip Buy the whole bracket's share in one go: 18 Weak Flux (18s) and Blacksmith Hammer (a tool: one, kept in your bags, 18c); about 18s 18c in all. The arrow picks the nearest seller of your faction (Stormwind City: Billibub Cogspinner, Brooke Stonebraid and Edna Mullby).
  buy 2880 x18 nearest
  buy 5956 nearest -- a tool, keep it in your bags

step Engineering 1-75: Auction House
  tip What 1-75 takes that the Auction House sells: 46 Rough Stone and 75 Copper Bar. The counts drop by what your bags, bank and mail hold.
  auction 2835 x46
  auction 2840 x75

